<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yue Fei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1103–1142</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yue Fei was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Southern Song</a> general who led campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> and its client state of Qi in the 1130s, recovering territory north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a>. Opposed to the peace policy of Emperor Gaozong and the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> Hui, he was recalled, imprisoned and executed around the time of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shaoxing">Treaty of Shaoxing</a>. He later became a national hero symbolising loyalty.</p></div>
